      "text": "To find the sum of the geometric series \\(1 + 2 + 4 + 8 + 16 + \\cdots + 1024\\), we first identify the first term and the common ratio of the series. The first term \\(a\\) is 1, and the common ratio \\(r\\) is 2.\n\nThe general form of the \\(n\\)-th term of a geometric series is given by:\n\\[ a_n = a \\cdot r^{n-1} \\]\nFor our series, the \\(n\\)-th term is:\n\\[ a_n = 2^{n-1} \\]\nWe need to find the number of terms \\(n\\) in the series. The last term is 1024, so we set up the equation:\n\\[ 2^{n-1} = 1024 \\]\nWe know that:\n\\[ 1024 = 2^{10} \\]\nThus:\n\\[ 2^{n-1} = 2^{10} \\]\nThis implies:\n\\[ n-1 = 10 \\]\n\\[ n = 11 \\]\nSo, there are 11 terms in the series.\n\nThe sum \\(S_n\\) of the first \\(n\\) terms of a geometric series is given by:\n\\[ S_n = a \\frac{r^n - 1}{r - 1} \\]\nSubstituting \\(a = 1\\), \\(r = 2\\), and \\(n = 11\\), we get:\n\\[ S_{11} = 1 \\cdot \\frac{2^{11} - 1}{2 - 1} = 2^{11} - 1 \\]\nWe calculate \\(2^{11}\\):\n\\[ 2^{11} = 2048 \\]\nTherefore:\n\\[ S_{11} = 2048 - 1 = 2047 \\]\nThe sum of the series \\(1 + 2 + 4 + 8 + 16 + \\cdots + 1024\\) is:\n\\[ \\boxed{2047} \\]",
