      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To solve the problem of finding the sum of the geometric series \\(1 + 2 + 4 + 8 + 16 + \\cdots + 1024\\), we need to identify the first term (\\(a\\)), the common ratio (\\(r\\)), and the number of terms (\\(n\\)) in the series.\n\n**Step 1: Identify the first term and the common ratio.**\nThe first term \\(a\\) is \\(1\\).\nThe common ratio \\(r\\) is the factor by which each term is multiplied to get the next term. From the series, we see that each term is half of the previous term. Therefore, \\(r = \\frac{1}{2}\\).\n\n**Step 2: Determine the number of terms in the series.**\nThe \\(n\\)-th term of a geometric series can be found using the formula:\n\\[ a_n = a \\cdot r^{n-1} \\]\nWe know the last term \\(a_n = 1024\\). So, we set up the equation:\n\\[ 1024 = 1 \\cdot \\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)^{n-1} \\]\nThis simplifies to:\n\\[ 1024 = \\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)^{n-1} \\]\nWe recognize that \\(1024 = 2^{10}\\), so:\n\\[ 2^{10} = \\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)^{n-1} \\]\nThis implies:\n\\[ 2^{10} = 2^{-n+1} \\]\nSince the bases are the same, we can equate the exponents:\n\\[ 10 = -n + 1 \\]\nSolving for \\(n\\):\n\\[ 10 + n = 1 \\]\n\\[ n = 11 \\]\nSo, there are 11 terms in the series.\n\n**Step 3: Use the formula for the sum of the first \\(n\\) terms of a geometric series.**\nThe sum \\(S_n\\) of the first \\(n\\) terms of a geometric series is given by:\n\\[ S_n = a \\frac{r^n - 1}{r - 1} \\]\nSubstituting \\(a = 1\\), \\(r = \\frac{1}{2}\\), and \\(n = 11\\):\n\\[ S_{11} = 1 \\cdot \\frac{\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)^{11} - 1}{\\frac{1}{2} - 1} \\]\n\\[ S_{11} = \\frac{\\frac{1}{2048} - 1}{-\\frac{1}{2}} \\]\n\\[ S_{11} = \\frac{\\frac{1}{2048} - \\frac{2048}{2048}}{-\\frac{1}{2}} \\]\n\\[ S_{11} = \\frac{-\\frac{2047}{2048}}{-\\frac{1}{2}} \\]\n\\[ S_{11} = \\frac{2047}{2048} \\cdot 2 \\]\n\\[ S_{11} = \\frac{2047}{1024} \\]\n\nTherefore, the sum of the series \\(1 + 2 + 4 + 8 + 16 + \\cdots + 1024\\) is \\(\\boxed{\\frac{2047}{1024}}\\).",
